Subject: load: mask forwarded store bits beyond the store width
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Base: c0818978acec60ebb6167fade60fb7012cbf20ca

When a load is partly forwarded from a narrower store that starts
before it, def() shifts the stored value right and only masks it when
the requested mask cuts the stored bits, or when the store ends before
the slice. The second test is right for left shifts but not for right
shifts, so bits of the stored value beyond the store width (an l temp
stored with storew, or a constant like -661 stored with storeh) were
kept and or'ed into the bytes defined by an older store:

	storel %a, %p
	storew %b, %p+2
	%v =w loaduh %p+5   # high byte of %b's low word, then a byte of %a

Mask whenever the shifted store bits do not reach the top of the
slice. Regression: filnix nanofil/tests/qbe-bugs/storew-l.ssa.

diff --git a/load.c b/load.c
index d7eaccb..5c96e08 100644
--- a/load.c
+++ b/load.c
@@ -313,7 +313,8 @@ def(Slice sl, bits msk, Blk *b, Ins *i, Loc *il)
 				r1 = getcon(8*off, curf);
 				r = iins(cls1, op, r, r1, il);
 			}
-			if ((msk1 & msk) != msk1 || off + sz < sl.sz)
+			if ((msk1 & msk) != msk1
+			|| (msk1 & BIT(8*sl.sz-1)) == 0)
 				mask(cls, &r, msk1 & msk, il);
 			if ((msk & ~msk1) != 0) {
 				r1 = def(sl, msk & ~msk1, b, i, il);
